msgstr "<0>price elasticity</0> ?"

msgid "<0>Resend</0> delivers our email."
msgstr "<0>Resend</0> delivers our email."

msgid "<0>Sign in with Apple</0> gives us your Apple account identifier, your email address (or a private relay address if you choose to hide yours) and, the first time, the name you agree to share. Without a name, we use the part of the email address before the “@”. We store the identity token Apple returns."
msgstr "<0>Sign in with Apple</0> gives us your Apple account identifier, your email address (or a private relay address if you choose to hide yours) and, the first time, the name you agree to share. Without a name, we use the part of the email address before the “@”. We store the identity token Apple returns."

msgid "<0>Sign in with Google</0> gives us your name, email address, profile photo and Google account identifier, along with the tokens Google returns. We copy the profile photo once to use as your picture in Lymi."
msgstr "<0>Sign in with Google</0> gives us your name, email address, profile photo and Google account identifier, along with the tokens Google returns. We copy the profile photo once to use as your picture in Lymi."

msgid "<0>Smart add (Anthropic)</0> reads the photos, PDFs and text you give it, with the names, descriptions and languages of up to 12 of your decks and a few recent terms and meanings from each. Photos are converted to WebP first, which removes metadata. Cloudflare Workers AI then checks the terms it found, and, if you ask, compares them with your answer. Lymi does not store the files: only the cards you choose to add are saved."
msgstr "<0>Smart add (Anthropic)</0> reads the photos, PDFs and text you give it, with the names, descriptions and languages of up to 12 of your decks and a few recent terms and meanings from each. Photos are converted to WebP first, which removes metadata. Cloudflare Workers AI then checks the terms it found, and, if you ask, compares them with your answer. Lymi does not store the files: only the cards you choose to add are saved."

msgid "<0>Sõber</0> sounds like “sober”: the friend who gets you home."
msgstr "<0>Sõber</0> sounds like “sober”: the friend who gets you home."

